course: dictionary
lesson: 4858
title: Words from the mountains
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ibex is a wild mountain goat with long, curved horns that have ridges on them. You can use ibex for one animal or for many: one ibex, two ibex, or ibexes. Some nouns, like this one, can stay the same in the plural.
explain: You can often work out a word from the words around it. «Alpine ibex climb the almost vertical stone walls of dams to lick salt.» Almost vertical means nearly straight up, and the walls are made of stone, so ibex must be animals that can climb very steep rock.
explain: Clues can also tell you what a word does. «Their hooves have hard edges and soft pads» tells you the feet are built to grip. Ask yourself: what would this animal need to be able to do for this sentence to make sense? When you still cannot tell, a dictionary settles it.
fact: An ibex is a wild mountain goat with long, curved, ridged horns.
fact: Ibexes live in steep, rocky places in Europe, Asia and North Africa.
fact: «Alpine ibex» and «Nubian ibex» are two kinds of ibex.
fact: «Ibex» is a noun, and it can mean one animal or many.
fact: Baby ibex can climb within days of being born.
exercise: What is an ibex? | A tall tree in a forest | A large fish with a long tail | *A wild mountain goat with long, curved horns | A small bird that lives near the sea
exercise: «Alpine ibex climb the almost vertical stone walls of dams to lick salt.» What does almost vertical mean? | *Nearly straight up and down | Covered in soft grass | Flat and level like a road | Slowly sloping down to a river
exercise: Which word in «Their hooves have hard edges and soft pads» names the body part that helps an ibex grip? | soft | have | *hooves | hard
test: Where are ibex most likely to be found? | *Steep, rocky mountains | Deep under the sea | Flat, empty places with no rocks | Busy city streets
test: «Baby ibex can climb within days of being born.» What does this tell you about ibex? | *They are born ready to climb | They climb very slowly at first | They cannot walk at all | They need help from humans to move
exam: What do the hard edges and soft pads on an ibex's hooves help it do? | Sing loudly to other animals | Fly over the valley | *Grip steep rock | Swim across rivers
